        "Section-6\n",
        "Discussion, limitation and the Future Work\n",
        "\n",
        "What design decision made the biggest difference ?\n",
        "In our above three iterations, feature selection (Itertion-2) and regularisationn (iteration-3) were the two design decision that stood out. The Baseline ( Iteration-1) ste a benck mark for what is achievable  without design choices. Removing features that were not strongly correlated with lacZ removed noise from the input . Regularisation with Dropout and BatchNorm in iteration-3 was designed to help generalise the data and prevent overfitting .\n",
        "\n",
        "Limitations:\n",
        "\n",
        "SMALL DATASET: with such a small number of observations(1000 sample and 45 features),we are at risk of overfitting ,especially with more complex model  .Nueral networks require many more observation to perform  to perform well compared to other machine learning algorithms.\n",
        "\n",
        "CORRELATION: Cporrelation not equal to causality, while lacA and lacY are highly correlated with lacZ,this does not imply causation . LacZ is regulated together with lacA and lacY within the same operon, hence they all are driven by a common signal upstarem\n",
        "\n",
        "LINEAR CORRELATION FOR FEATURES SELECTION: our correlation method selects only liner relationship.Any gene that shows non-lenier effect in lacZ Expression will be missed using our approach .\n",
        "\n",
        "MANUALCHOICE OF HYPERPARAMETERS: choosing learning rates and architecture sizes manually ca be imoroved with automatic approaches(i.e k-fold cross-validation)\n",
        "\n",
        "FUTURE Work:\n",
        "\n",
        "CROSS-VALIDATION: Perform k-fold cross-validation rather than using just one training/validation/test partition.\n",
        "Ensemble models: Ensemble models (averaging results from several predictions from different models) reduce variance of the predictions.\n",
        "NON-LENIER FEATURE SELECTION : Use Random Forest to calculate feature importance rather than plain correlation for non-linear gene relationships.\n",
        "COLLECT MORE DATA : More experimental data would allow the neural network to perform better than any simpler regression algorithms."
      ]
    }
